# .gitignore for the mirasol2026 release.
#
# Two rules govern this file, and both were violated by the development tree
# this release was extracted from:
#
#   1. Large binaries and third-party data must NEVER be committed. One ONNX
#      graph here is 109.4 MiB, above GitHub's 100 MiB hard blob limit, and the
#      CirCor DigiScope metadata is not ours to redistribute.
#   2. The small artefacts that make the paper reproducible from a clean clone
#      MUST be committed, even when a broad pattern above would swallow them.
#      Those are re-included by negation below and are checked in CI with
#      `git check-ignore -v`.
#
# If you add a pattern, re-run the CI check: a silent over-broad rule is how
# the benchmark input, the quantization logs and all 61 prediction CSVs came to
# be excluded from the original repository.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Model artefacts (published as GitHub Release assets, never committed)
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Anchored to the repository root on purpose: an unanchored `models/` rule would
# also ignore src/mirasol/models/, which is source code.
/exports/
/models/
deployment/edge/models/
*.onnx
*.onnx.data
*.ort
sym_shape_infer_temp.onnx
*_temp.onnx

# ONNX Runtime quantization residue. The UUID-named .data files embed the
# generating machine's NIC MAC address in their filename; sym_shape_infer_temp
# embeds absolute paths from the generating venv. Never commit either.
# (This pattern anchors at the end of the name, so results/predictions/*.data.csv
# is unaffected.)
*.data

# Training checkpoints (26 GB of them in the development tree; the release
# ships results/checkpoint_accuracies.csv instead)
*.ckpt
*.pt
*.pth
*.safetensors

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Data. CirCor DigiScope is ODC-By and is NOT redistributed here: see
# data/README.md. `data/*` is deliberately single-level so that re-including
# data/splits/ below actually works - git cannot re-include a file whose parent
# directory is excluded.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
data/*
!data/README.md
!data/splits/
data/splits/*
!data/splits/*.csv
!data/splits/README.md

# Prepared datasets and raw audio anywhere in the tree (1.66 GiB per .npy
# configuration, 81 GB of WAVs)
*.npy
*.npz
*.wav
*.flac
*.h5
*.hdf5
# ...except the synthetic Table 4 benchmark input: RandomState(42) noise plus
# 50/120 Hz sinusoids, 512,384 B, no patient data, and the only input to the
# on-device benchmark. Without it Table 4 is unreproducible from a clean clone.
!deployment/edge/bench_input.npy

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Run outputs
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
/runs/
/outputs/
lightning_logs/
tb_logs/
events.out.tfevents.*
*.log
# ...except the three logs that are the only surviving evidence for the FP16
# agreement, the static-INT8 collapse and the QAT run.
!results/logs/*.log

# Analysis outputs are regenerated, not committed - with the exception of the
# committed prediction dumps and benchmark JSONs under results/.
figures/
/fig/
*.pdf
!docs/**/*.pdf

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Python
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*$py.class
*.so
.Python
build/
dist/
*.egg-info/
.eggs/
.installed.cfg
.pytest_cache/
.ruff_cache/
.mypy_cache/
.coverage
.coverage.*
htmlcov/
.tox/
.nox/

# Virtual environments
venv/
.venv/
env/
ENV/

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Editors, agents, notebooks and scratch (all carried machine-identifying
# paths or credentials in the development tree)
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
.claude/
.idea/
.vscode/
*.iml
notebooks/
.ipynb_checkpoints/
*.ipynb
temp/
tmp/
scratch/
scratch_*.py

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# OS and misc
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
*.~lock*
*.swp
*~
